From 034d460e8acebe00c0fbb3f6614262254aed23a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 01:25:26 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panthor: try named gpu_core ACPI clock before bare NULL
 lookup (NCZ 0086)

Forward-port of our own 7.0.12-cix-sky1-next fix
(2012-fix-panthor-gate-Sky1-gpu_core-clock-fallback.patch, already
shipping and confirmed working), never carried into the 7.1/7.2 series.

panthor_clk_init() tries devm_clk_get(dev, NULL) (bare/default clock)
first. On Sky1 ACPI boot the CIXH5000 GPU device clock is registered
under the ACPI clkdev name gpu_core, not as a default/NULL lookup --
confirmed on real hardware tonight:

  panthor CIXH5000:00: error -ENOENT: get core clock failed
  panthor CIXH5000:00: probe with driver panthor failed with error -2

Fix: when the bare lookup fails AND the device has an ACPI companion
matching CIXH5000, try the named gpu_core lookup before giving up.
Falls through to the original error path unchanged if that also fails.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_device.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_device.c
index 793a24bb783d..ea33b6366a7e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panthor/panthor_device.c
@@ -32,6 +32,9 @@
 static int panthor_clk_init(struct panthor_device *ptdev)
 {
 	ptdev->clks.core = devm_clk_get(ptdev->base.dev, NULL);
+	if (IS_ERR(ptdev->clks.core) && has_acpi_companion(ptdev->base.dev) &&
+	    acpi_dev_hid_match(ACPI_COMPANION(ptdev->base.dev), "CIXH5000"))
+		ptdev->clks.core = devm_clk_get_optional(ptdev->base.dev, "gpu_core");
 	if (IS_ERR(ptdev->clks.core))
 		return dev_err_probe(ptdev->base.dev,
 				     PTR_ERR(ptdev->clks.core),
-- 
